        # ReleaseNotes of this module
        ReleaseNotes = 'v0.11.3: SAFETY: rm -rf "$unset" (an empty operand) no longer deletes the current directory''s contents (data loss in 0.11.2); every command treats an empty path as missing. The host now survives hostile input (deep nesting, huge chains, brace bombs, catastrophic regexes, runaway recursion and memory, kill -9 $$): only that command fails, and every host exit is logged with a reason. Fixes: heredocs and parens inside "$(...)" (git commit -m "$(cat <<''EOF'' ...)" with it''s or :) failed to parse); set -e stops on any failing command; if/while conditions keep their output; || and && see return N; subshells no longer leak set -e, variables or shopt; >&2 obeys 2>/dev/null and 2>&1; 2> files are byte-exact; repeated redirects; a failed redirect never runs its command; grep/sed BRE \| \( \{ \+ \?; expr :; extglob in case and [[ ]]; literal and expanded /tmp paths agree; date +%N; concurrent commands in the codex sandbox; locked files report Permission denied. v0.11.2: fixes a v0.11.0 regression where every native command (git, wsl, tman...) hung under an agent shell tool whose stdin is open but never written: natives now get the shell stdin as a real OS pipe, and what they do not read stays for the next command. Also: cmd < /dev/null means empty input; cd/eval/source/read/set keep their redirects; declare/typeset -f/-F/-p implemented (no more type: -f: not found); command -v, type and which print bash names instead of Invoke-Bash* and follow bash exit codes; BASH_VERSION and --version report the real version instead of 0.8.0. v0.11.1: maintenance — zero compiler warnings in PsBash.Core.Tests (nullability, xUnit analyzers, platform attributes, a duplicate test case removed) and a much smaller agent instruction context. v0.11.0: GNU-parity release. One shared ordered argument parser now drives ~50 commands (bundles, --, unique-prefix long options, GNU usage errors; a real option ps-bash does not implement is refused with exit 2, never silently ignored). Shell semantics: pathname expansion is a shell step (echo *, for f in *, arrays), $(...) word-splits, : > f creates the file, env prefixes reach pipe stages, compound commands share stdin, the launcher forwards its stdin into -c. Binary-safe bytes end to end (cat of a binary file is byte-exact; printf ''\351'' | wc -c is 1). Commands: find (-printf, -perm, -user, -newerXY, -L ...), grep/rg/sed option sets, ls layouts and sorting, cut -c in bytes, split -n, sort -R/-z/-V suffixes, join -o/-e, uniq --group, cat -A, head/tail -v/-z/-F, wc --total, cp/mv -i/-t/-T/-b/--update, ln -r, tar member filters, GNU diff options, a new jq engine with --arg/-n/-e, awk getline/print redirection/functions. Streaming and memory: grep/sed/find/tail/awk/seq/redirect stream with bounded memory; the host frees output as it is sent. Host: warm nested daemons per depth, cached command-not-found index (missing command 9s -> 1s). Linux/macOS fixes. Intentional differences: docs/specs/intentional-differences.md. v0.10.23: Daemon stall fix, release-archive fix, and a transpiler correctness batch from a real-world .sh corpus sweep. Host: a command whose launcher died mid-flight kept running in the daemon while holding the process-wide execution gate, so every later command in that session queued behind work nobody would ever read — a launcher killed 2s into sleep 30 made the next command wait 30.9s; now 0.2s. Connections now detect client disconnect (EOF, on live duplex transports only) and cancel the abandoned command, and WorkerPool.DisposeAsync awaits in-flight warmers so no runspace outlives its pool. Packaging: every release archive since v0.9.1 shipped without System.Management.Automation.dll and failed every command with "ps-bash-host did not accept connections within 20s" — PrivateAssets=all on the Microsoft.PowerShell.SDK reference excluded the SDK runtime assets from publish. Fixed, and build.yml plus publish.yml now RUN the packaged archive (scripts/smoke-archive.ps1) before uploading, which no workflow previously did. Transpiler, every fix oracle-verified against bash: command substitution as an arithmetic operand, $(( $(date +%s) + 60 )); empty case-arm bodies no longer swallow their own terminator; [[ x =~ ^(a|b)$ ]] keeps its regex; array literals spanning newlines, and declare/readonly/local initializers, survive; here-strings on compound commands; single-item for-in; while read a b binds every name; [[ ( … ) ]] grouping; quoted test operands keep expansions live; compound commands as &&/|| operands; braced ${name} before a colon; nested quotes inside "$( … )"; $(<file). Runtime: POSIX bracket classes such as [[:digit:]] and [[:space:]] never worked in grep/sed/awk/rg and silently matched nothing — they are now translated for .NET; binder-swallowed-flag recovery no longer reads a different pipeline stage. v0.10.21: Robustness & security batch from a four-subsystem code review (37 findings). Transpiler: expanding-heredoc command substitutions $(...) and backticks are now transpiled instead of executed as raw PowerShell (a quoting-seam code-execution leak), with backslash escapes honoured; quote-aware ${...} boundary scanning; brace-expansion items escaped via PsBuild; subshell input redirects (cmd) < file; and a class of parser crashes now emits a clean positioned error instead (lone here-string quote, out-of-range fd, for $i, empty redirect target, ${10000000000}, oversized brace tuples). BashArith hex/octal literals wrap at 64 bits instead of throwing. Cmdlets: the entire PowerShell common-parameter binder-collision cluster is resolved — every colliding short flag (cp/mv/rm -i, cat -A/-v, column -o/-c, tee -p, tree -p/-C, split -e/-C, strings -a/-e, grep -d/-D, sort -i, head/tail -v, du -P, uniq -w, readlink -e/-v, mktemp -p) now binds a decoy parameter so it no longer crashes the binder or silently drops, with the collision guard extended to catch the class mechanically; column -s with an empty separator no longer splits per character; tail -f withholds a partial final line until its newline arrives. Host/shell: Ctrl-C no longer races the prompt-loop token dispose into a process crash; Tab completion is deadline-bounded so it never hangs; the alias table is concurrency-safe; completion columns use display width; POSIX cwd tracking, scrollback preservation on a clean non-zero exit, and frecency-store disposal on the connection-lost path are fixed; ps-bash -c cmd --version now runs the command instead of printing the banner. Core/IPC: the stale-artifact reaper unlink race and a ModuleExtractor winner mis-handling are closed; the post-EXIT read is deadline-bounded; a persistent spawn-lock permission error degrades to an unguarded spawn instead of a 20s stall; compact output flushes a partial digest on a transport reset; a CommandNameCache lost-wakeup is fixed. v0.10.20: Robustness, correctness & security batch (issues #5-#17). Emitter: guard empty-Words so malformed <( / $( no longer crashes; bind while-read loop vars by assignment not text-rewrite; drop leading/trailing empty fields from unquoted word-split; expand ${x:-fallback} inside expanding heredocs; escape single quotes at the bash/PS seam; var-in-command-position and array/subscript expansion; bare Windows drive paths (C:\...) resolve in cd. Runtime: escape jq/yq JSON object keys and resolve jq negative index per item; correct Test-BashCondition -a/-o precedence and binary primaries; ps entries report the real PID and leaked process-sub temp files are swept; align __BashLastCwd init so chpwd does not fire on first prompt. Cmdlets: correct sed BRE escape translation; fix traceroute deadlock, dangling-symlink ls crash, read-only install/rmdir, grep -o multi-match; clamp joined-flag numeric parses to stop int.Parse overflow; mktemp exclusive-create 0600. IPC/host: serialize requests so the OutputCallback swap is race-free; stop orphaning slow hosts and retire the daemon under the spawn lock; cap the compact-output intake buffer with streaming degrade; cancel-stop runaway ExecuteAsync and guard a disposed pool. Shell: wait for runspace readiness before alias expansion; unfreeze the prompt on a dead/stalled frecency path; new gtui interactive git-status TUI. Security: redact value-flag/URL secrets, make AI command assist opt-in and broaden redaction, stop cp -r/find/tar -c following directory junctions; CI gates the build on security probes. v0.10.19: psgit + styled filesystem view. New Invoke-BashGit (alias psgit) renders git as structured PowerShell objects — status/log/branch/remote/tag/stash list/diff parse into typed PsBash.Git* objects you can filter, sort, and pipe; other subcommands pass through to native git, which stays untouched and fully interactive (psgit is deliberately NOT aliased to git). psgit reuses your configured git auth (SSH agent + cached/stored credential helpers) non-interactively; GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 makes terminal-prompt auth fail fast instead of hanging. The structured objects ship everywhere; piping to Show-Styled / Format-Styled git colours them by state (Strata-gated). Get-ChildItem | Format-Styled fs now renders a curated, human-oriented table — a file-type emoji + name, a human size with a visual size meter, and a relative modified time — coloured by type, instead of dumping every property. Format-Styled now honours an object''s DefaultDisplayPropertySet (the same curated columns Format-Table uses), so any typed object shows sensible columns. v0.10.18: Interactive shell + transpiler fixes. The type-ahead command panel now lists live PowerShell commands (cmdlets/functions/aliases from loaded modules), background-preloaded once the runspace is ready and refreshed after each command so a just-defined function/alias shows up without a Tab round-trip. Path-like .sh/.bash scripts (./build.sh, dir/x.sh, /abs/x.sh) now run through bash — they execute correctly AND compose in a pipeline instead of failing with "Cannot run a document in the middle of a pipeline". Format-Styled/Show-Styled stylesheets use the .pcss extension (the ps-bash CSS-like dialect with Strata Kind selectors and command: bindings); user overrides prefer <name>.pcss with a .css fallback. SQLitePCLRaw bundle bumped to 3.0.3 to clear the NU1903 advisory (GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q, now covering the whole 2.1.x line) that broke the AOT /warnaserror build. Full version history with complete per-release detail: CHANGELOG.md in the repo and https://github.com/standardbeagle/ps-bash/releases'

    } # End of PSData hashtable

} # End of PrivateData hashtable

